# CyberMyth OS amd64 build tree
#
# Everything that defines the build is TRACKED: the scripts, the kernel config
# and its fragments, branding assets, Calamares overrides, the archive keyring
# and the docs. Only regenerable outputs are ignored, and every one of them can
# be rebuilt by a script in this tree.
#
# Rough sizes at the time of writing, for context on why each is excluded:
#   linux-6.18.49/   32 GB    rootfs/  5.9 GB    iso-work/  2.4 GB
#   *.iso           2.4 GB    pkg/     1.8 GB

# --- Kernel ------------------------------------------------------------------
# The extracted upstream source tree and the object tree bindeb-pkg leaves in
# it. Re-extract the upstream tarball and run kernel/build-kernel.sh.
linux-*/
kernel/build.log
# Intermediate configs kept for debugging a config regression. The FINAL config
# lives at kernel/config-cybermyth-amd64 and IS tracked -- it is the reviewable
# artefact, and nothing here ignores it.
kernel/staged/

# --- Packages ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Kernel .debs (~1.2 GB incl. the -dbg package)  -> kernel/build-kernel.sh
# tor-browser .deb (133 MB)                      -> pkg/build-tor-browser.sh
# firmware .debs (307 MB)                        -> pkg/fetch-firmware.sh
# arch-split firmware .debs                      -> pkg/rearch-firmware.sh
*.deb
pkg/

# --- Root filesystem ---------------------------------------------------------
# sudo ./mk-rootfs.sh   (rootfs.state records which stages completed)
rootfs/
rootfs.state

# --- ISO ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# sudo ./mk-iso.sh
iso-work/
*.iso
*.iso.sha256

# --- Local scratch -----------------------------------------------------------
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
tmp
*.swp
*~
build.md
